Text editor for every input in the Text state, per HTML's type attribute rules (Roves).

Base: crates.io blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.4 (DioxusLabs/blitz
92b11f1bd8ab7975411328b0406a95a09445b4e7, packages/blitz-dom), after 0001 and 0002.
Applied in support/blitz-v8-probe/vendor/blitz-dom; see ROVES_PATCHES.md there.

The `type` attribute is ASCII case-insensitive and its missing/invalid value default is
the Text state. Blitz matched the raw attribute against literal keywords, so an
`<input type="string">` (visual-novel-template's name prompt, Pixi'VN
`requestInput({ type: "string" })`) or `type="TEXT"` got no text editor and could not
be typed into.

